<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEDAL ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEDAL ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the medal round at the ice hockey world championships on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Canada 1 Finland 0 (0-0 0-0 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Jeff Friesen (56:33)</p>
<p>Penalties: Canada 10 minutes, Finland 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,298  </p>
<p>Russia 1 United States 1 (0-0 0-1 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Russia - Alexei Morozov (53:49)</p>
<p>United States - Marty McInnis (37:02)</p>
<p>Penalties: Russia 8 minutes, U.S. 8</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,197</p>
<p>    Standings	  P   W  D  L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Russia	     4   2  1  1  12  11    5</p>
<p> 2. Sweden	     3   2  0  1  11   7    4</p>
<p> 3. Canada	     3   2  0  1   8   8    4</p>
<p> 4. United States    4   1  1  2   7  12    3</p>
<p> 5. Finland	    3   1  0  2   8   7    2</p>
<p> 6. Czech Republic   3   1  0  2   7   8    2</p>
<p>Next matches: May 7 - Canada v Czech Republic, Sweden v</p>
<p>Finland</p>
